0..78 Comment "//! `cancelled-receiver` models a peer that waits after a handler abandons its"
79..96 Comment "//! continuation."
97..100 Comment "//!"
101..166 Comment "//! The abandoned rest holds an end whose protocol is still open."
167..212 Comment "//! So the rest owes its peer a cancellation."
213..288 Comment "//! It proves that a waiting peer observes cancellation at its next action."
289..337 Comment "//! The peer then abandons its own continuation."
338..388 Comment "//! An abandoned end also cancels each queued end."
389..392 Comment "//!"
393..443 Comment "//! Each program exits from its root continuation."
444..487 Comment "//! The handler abandons that continuation."
488..507 Comment "//! It returns `7`."
508..511 Comment "//!"
512..553 Comment "//! - see: #3305 — the cancellation hop"
554..636 Comment "//! - cites: [Fowler-2019-exceptional_asynchronous_session_types] — cancellation"
637..707 Comment "//!   reaching the peer and every end left in a cancelled end\'s buffer"
708..711 Comment "//!"
712..878 Comment "//! [Fowler-2019-exceptional_asynchronous_session_types]: https://doi.org/10.1145/3290341 \"Fowler, Lindley, Morris and Decova, Exceptional Asynchronous Session Types\""
880..933 Comment "// The import provides the early-exit host interface."
